  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Appraisal of two projects to promote economic resilience through increased trade and integration in East and West Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The appraisal concern two regional projects aimed to boost Africa&#x2019;s resilience to economic challenges by promoting trade and economic integration in a changing geopolitical context. The projects will have a particular focus on East and West Africa and will be referred to combined the &#x2018;Increased Trade and Regional Integration in Africa, support to the East African Community (EAC) and the Economic Community of West African States (ECOWAS) (ITREIA)&#x2019;. 

The appraisal is of a program, that is intended to have a total commitment of DKK 80 million over three years and will be a key initiative focusing on regional trade in line with the new Danish Africa Strategy &#x2013; Africa&#x2019;s Century and Denmark&#x2019;s Strategy for Development Cooperation &#x2013; A Changing World Partnerships in Development. ITEREIA is also a direct response to growing global trade volatility, including the effects of US-China trade disputes and changes to the African Growth and Opportunity Act (AGOA).</narrative>
  </description>
